{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--complement-head-lacks-internal-role","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--arity-zero"],"statement":{"en":"In a complement clause construction, the nominal head only nominalizes the entire clause without having a grammatical role inside it.","ja":"補文構造において、主要部名詞は節全体を名詞化するだけであり、節内部で文法的な役割を持たない。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0503-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--noun-complements-lack-internal-gap","differs_in":"framework","note":"Both formulate the absence of an internal gap or syntactic role within the complement clause, using arity-0 versus general syntactic terms."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--uske-usi-complementizer-and-relative-head","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--arity-zero"],"statement":{"en":"The nouns uske and usi function both as complementizers when preceded by an arity-0 complete clause and as relative clause heads when preceded by an incomplete clause.","ja":"名詞 uske および usi は、先行節がアリティ0の完結文である場合は補文標識として、不完結な節である場合は関係節の主要部として両機能にまたがって用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["uske","usi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0505-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--zero-nominalization-precedes-overt-nominalizers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--bare-complementation"],"statement":{"en":"Zero-nominalization represents the oldest stratum of nominalization in Ainu, while nominalizing words developed later.","ja":"アイヌ語においてゼロ名詞化は名詞化の最も古い段階を反映しており、名詞化語を用いる方策は後代に生じた。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"epistemic","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2016@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-02","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--prolative-infinitive-bare-verb","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--bare-complementation"],"statement":{"en":"In prolative infinitive constructions, Class II verbs appear in their bare form without personal affixes.","ja":"いわゆる prolative infinitive 構造において、第II類動詞は人称接辞を伴わない裸の形態で用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["prolative infinitive construction"]},"forms":["chish"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0083-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--complementizer-choice-governed-by-matrix-predicate","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--complement-predicates"],"statement":{"en":"The selection of a complementizer depends on discourse context and the semantic class of the matrix predicate.","ja":"補文標識の選択は文脈および主節述語の意味論的クラスに依存する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0021-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--predicate-variation-overt-vs-zero-nominalization","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--complement-predicates"],"statement":{"en":"Certain complement-taking predicates require overt nominalizers such as hi or pe, whereas others allow zero-nominalization.","ja":"補文をとる述語には hi や pe などの明示的な名詞化語を要求するものがある一方で、ゼロ名詞化を許容するものもある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["hi","pe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2016@pdftotext-pieces/l0005-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--complement-clause-grammatical-relations","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--constituency"],"statement":{"en":"Complement clauses in Ainu can function syntactically as S or O, and rarely as A.","ja":"アイヌ語の補文節は統語的にSまたはOとして機能し、まれにAとして機能する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0021-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--noun-complement-clause-as-possessive","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--constituency"],"statement":{"en":"Noun complement clauses pattern syntactically as possessive noun phrases, with the modifying clause serving as the possessor and referent for possessive marking on the head.","ja":"名詞補文節は所属名詞句と同様のパターンをとり、修飾節全体が主要部の所属標示に対する所有者および指示対象として機能する。"},"type":"analysis","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0007-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--interrogative-complementizer-restricted-to-ya","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--indirect-speech-complementizers"],"statement":{"en":"The use of interrogative particles as complementizers is restricted to ya.","ja":"補文標識として用いられる疑問小詞は ya に限られる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ya"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0330-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--noun-complements-lack-internal-gap","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Noun complement clauses in Ainu lack an internal syntactic gap and have no underlying base clause.","ja":"アイヌ語の名詞補文節は節内部に空所を持たず、基底となる基本節を欠く。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0007-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--evidential-nouns-as-complementizers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--sensory-complementizers"],"statement":{"en":"Noun complement clauses employ a paradigm of possessive evidential forms as complementizers, including ru-w-e, haw-e, sir-i, and hum-i.","ja":"名詞補文節は、ru-w-e、haw-e、sir-i、hum-i などの所属形をとる証拠的意味を持つ一連の形式を補文標識として用いる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ru-w-e","haw-e","sir-i","hum-i"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0007-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--evidentials-function-as-complement-markers","differs_in":null,"note":"Specifies the particular inventory of possessive evidential nouns (ru-w-e, haw-e, sir-i, hum-i) acting as complementizers."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--evidentials-function-as-complement-markers","revision":1,"topic":"topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topics":["topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising","topic:complex/nominalized-complements-control-raising--sensory-complementizers"],"statement":{"en":"Evidential markers in Ainu function as complement clause markers.","ja":"アイヌ語において、証拠性標識は補文標識として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:takahashi2022@handbook-epub/l0122-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
